  "strategy": "1. Approach and Rationale\nWe develop a strategy to minimize the AC1 upper bound by combining frequency-domain analysis and gradient-based optimization. The central idea is to leverage the relationship between signal properties in the time and frequency domains to systematically identify sequences with lower autocorrelation properties. \n\nThe core bottleneck in previous approaches was the non-convex optimization landscape and the curse of dimensionality for long sequences (384 elements). Our solution involves:\n- Using frequency-domain initialization to guide the search\n- Employing gradient-based optimization with careful step control\n- Incorporating dimension compression to balance exploration and exploitation\n- Maintaining tight slack terms to stabilize optimization\n- Using adaptive resampling to maintain sequence length and support size\n\nOur rationale is that sequences with compact frequency support tend to have favorable autocorrelation properties, and we can leverage this insight to guide the optimization process.\n\nThis plan is scientific guidance, not a binding specification. You may correct, adapt, simplify, or replace components when justified by the task.\n\n2. Mathematical Specification\n- Variables: Non-negative coefficients a_i (0 \u2264 a_i \u2264 1000)\n- Representation: Real-valued coefficient vector of dimension n\n- Objective: Minimize 2n\u00b7max(\u2202(a)) / (\u2211a_i)\u00b2, where \u2202(a) is the full autocorrelation\n- Constraints:\n  - Non-negativity: a_i \u2265 0 for all i\n  - Upper bound: a_i \u2264 1000 for all i\n  - Minimum support: \u2211a_i \u2265 0.01  \n- Formulation:  \n  Let \u2202_k = \u03a3\u1d62 a\u1d62\u00b7a\u208d\u208e for k = 0 to 2n-2  \n  The objective is f(a) = 2n\u00b7max_k(\u2202_k) / (S_a)\u00b2\n- Optimization: We use proximal gradient descent with:\n  - Line searches with backtracking\n  - Cauchy sequence projection\n  - Dimension compression via sampling\n  - Variable slack to handle constraints\n\n3. Implementation Procedure\n- Initialization:  \n  1. Start with a cosine-based initialization if parent available  \n  2. If not, initialize with normalized uniform distribution  \n\n- Optimization Loop:  \n  for iteration in range(max_iter):  \n    1. Compute current autocorrelation  \n    2. Identify active constraints  \n    3. Compute projected gradient  \n    4. Perform line search with adaptive step size  \n    5. Update coefficients with projected gradient  \n    6. Apply dimension compression to maintain support size  \n    7. Check termination conditions  \n\n- Helper Functions:  \n  - autocorrelation(a): Fast convolution via FFT  \n  - update_with_slack(x, grad, step_size): Apply directional update with slack  \n  - compress_representation(x, compression_factor): Sample elements of the sequence  \n\n- Termination:  \n  - Function evaluation exceeds budget  \n  - Gradient norm below tolerance  \n  - Value stabilizes across iterations  \n\n4. Search Choices and Useful Variations  \n- Default configuration:  \n  \u2022 Initial sampling: 128 elements  \n  \u2022 Step size: 0.5  \n  \u2022 Line search epsilon: 0.1  \n  \u2022 Compression factor: 0.8  \n  \u2022 Gradient tolerance: 1e-4  \n\n- Triggered adjustments:  \n  \u00b0 For high dimension: Activate compression (factor 0.6)  \n  \u00b0 For poor progress: Increase step size (to 0.7)  \n  \u00b0 For unfavorable scores: Switch to conservative initialization  \n\n5. Compute Budget and Robustness  \n- Phases:  \n  \u2022 Exploration: 400 seconds (50% of budget)  \n  \u2022 Refinement: 600 seconds (75% of budget)  \n  \u2022 Validation: 200 seconds (25% of budget)  \n\n- Time management:  \n  \u00b0 Check elapsed time before each expensive operation  \n  \u00b0 Reduce budget usage by 20% for projected gradient steps  \n  \u00b0 Break early for terminal condition  \n\n- Fallback for failures:  \n  \u00b0 Maintain minimal sequence if evaluation fails  \n  \u00b0 Retain parent sequence if complete optimization fails  \n  \u00b0 Default to gradient-stable initialization  \n\n6. Validation and Return Contract  \n- Candidate selection:  \n  \u00b0 Validate each candidate with exact evaluator  \n  \u00b0 Track lowest-fitness sequence  \n  \u00b0 Verify final candidate has finite, low score  \n\n- Post-processing:  \n  \u00b0 Compute final score with evaluator  \n  \u00b0 Ensure normalized sum \u2265 0.01  \n  \u00b0 Clip values to [0,1000] before evaluation  \n\n- Success criteria:  \n  \u00b0 Score < 1.5]  \n  \u00b0 Competitive with parent's score",
